    "id": "2a3b4c5d6e7f8091",
    "type": "comment",
    "z": "1a2b3c4d5e6f7081",
    "name": "Centrifuge: request (rpc, history, presence)",
    "info": "Prerequisites: a Centrifugo v6 server on ws://localhost:8000. The repository ships one: edit quickstart/centrifugo.yaml (set client.token.hmac_secret_key), then run `centrifugo --config quickstart/centrifugo.yaml`.\n\nOpen the `centrifuge server` configuration, paste the server's `client.token.hmac_secret_key` into Secret, and deploy.\n\nHistory and presence stats work with the quick-start config as shipped. RPC needs an RPC proxy: uncomment the `rpc:` block in quickstart/centrifugo.yaml (it forwards to an HTTP backend you provide at the given endpoint) before clicking the RPC inject, otherwise it fails with `SERVER_ERROR` (server code 108, \"not available\").\n\nExpected: `history news` returns `{ publications, offset, epoch }` for channel `news`; `presence stats news` returns `{ numUsers, numClients }`; `rpc echo` calls your RPC backend's `echo` method with `{\"hello\":\"world\"}` and returns its response. Errors from any of the three route to the Catch node.",
    "x": 200,
    "y": 40,
    "wires": []
  },
  {
